dialect protocol
protocol stdio.semio.document.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.semio.document
start body
framing record

# ARTIFACT-SYSTEM-OVERHAUL-REAL-CODECS-RUNTIME-REUSE-EVOLUTION document wave: REAL binary op
# frame, replacing the old `print_op().into_bytes()` text-as-binary shortcut
# (`🧬️mutations/🦀️.rs`'s old `OpBinary::encode_op`). `SemioDocumentMutation` is a
# genuine data-carrying enum whose variants embed a nested, recursive `DocBlock`/
# `SemioDocumentSnapshot` payload — no `dsl::DslField` impl exists for the tagged `DocBlock` enum
# (hand-rolled per this subset's own `🔺️diff`/`🧬️mutations` convention), so the generic
# derive-based `format u8 | ordinal varint | record body` layout doesn't apply. Handcrafted
# instead: `format u8` (`OP_BINARY_FORMAT` convention) + `tag u8` (the `SemioDocumentMutation`
# variant ordinal, `🧬️mutations/🦀️.rs`'s `OP_KEYWORDS`/`variant_ordinal`, same 0-17
# ordering as `parse_document_mutation`'s keyword match) as two REAL fixed fields, then the
# variant's own `key=value ...` argument payload as one opaque trailing `bytes` chain — the same
# honest boundary the sibling `../../🔺️diff/💾️binary/📡️.protocol.semio` uses
# (`protocol-array-of-records`/`protocol-prim-ref-recursion`, per the recipe's gap table).
header fixed 2
field format u8
field tag u8

chain payload bytes
